{"id":"odu-run-dies-with-mcp-host","parent":"oduc-runs","ord":"a3","title":"PR: a run started from odu's MCP dies with its host, and says so","done":"2026-09-02T20:33:18-04:00","started":"2026-09-02T19:12:08-04:00","worked":4870,"desc":"Seen 2026-09-02 19:02–19:04 ET: the orchestrator started `run` on .worktrees/cordis-server through the olai chat's odu MCP (`.ci/25d1532/` created, `odu.sock` bound); the human redeployed olai at 19:04:29 and the coordinator was gone with it — a detached child is still in the service's cgroup, and systemd kills the cgroup on stop — leaving a stale `odu.run.lock` and socket, `runs` answering an empty ledger, no settle and no CI chip. The MCP tool's description promises the coordinator \"keeps going even if this MCP server exits or is restarted\", which is false under a service restart.\n\nRULED by the human 2026-09-02 ~19:12 ET: ADMIT THE LIMIT, do not escape the cgroup. So: (1) the `run` tool's description and answer say the coordinator lives and dies with its host process — a restart of the host kills the run; (2) a stale lock and socket with no live coordinator are reported as \"a run died here at <sha>\" by `runs`, `wait_for_settle` and the CI doorbell, never as an empty ledger; (3) the orchestrator's own practice: relaunch after any deploy. Not chosen: `systemd-run --scope` to outlive the host.","created":"2026-09-02T19:09:16-04:00","changed":"2026-09-02T20:33:18-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-opencode","brief":"briefs/odu-run-dies-with-host.md","dispatched":"2026-09-02T19:15:00-04:00","from":"the orchestrator, 2026-09-02 19:06 ET, after the human's deploy of #474 killed #474's own CI run","kolu-terminal":"9b6ffe9a","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/odu/commit/210b1710","merged":"2026-09-02","musts":"2","odu-worktree":".worktrees/run-dies-with-host","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/odu/pull/98","repo":"repo-odu","tier":"mechanical","timings":"implement 32m red-first (opencode) · review 9m (grok, 2 MUST 4 SHOULD) · address 14m · re-verdict 4m · merge-master skipped · ci 1m51s both platforms 18/18 · merge <1m — TOTAL 1h17m (19:15 → 20:32 ET)"}}
