{"id":"lane-ordh-address","parent":"odu-run-dies-with-mcp-host","ord":"a3","title":"address findings","done":"2026-09-02T20:14:35-04:00","started":"2026-09-02T19:59:31-04:00","worked":904,"after":["lane-ordh-review-a"],"created":"2026-09-02T19:11:57-04:00","changed":"2026-09-02T20:14:35-04:00"}
{"id":"lane-ordh-ci","parent":"odu-run-dies-with-mcp-host","ord":"a4","title":"CI green at head — both platforms","done":"2026-09-02T20:30:02-04:00","started":"2026-09-02T20:19:53-04:00","worked":609,"desc":"Run 4d1dc5b#1 on both platforms: every node green at 20:21 ET (18/18; darwin on petit, linux on kolu-ci-5). NO SETTLE RANG IN THE CHAT, and the cause is verified, not the one first written here: the orchestrator launched this run with `linger`, and olai-plugin-odu's CI doorbell says \"settled\" only when the run's socket dies (packages/odu-client/src/runs.ts: the settle IS the socket's death); a lingering coordinator keeps the socket open until its idle reap (~30 min — #474's run 3 rang its settle at 19:51 ET, when its lingering coordinator reaped, though its nodes had finished by 19:22). The path resolution was never the problem: `worktreeAt` places a relative value under `<reposRoot>/<repo>/` with the repo from the PR URL or the file's projects/<repo>/ prefix, and this row has both. Remedy: cancel the lingering coordinator so the socket dies and the settle rings; never launch with `linger` on a lane the doorbell watches.","after":["lane-ordh-merge-master","lane-ordh-address"],"created":"2026-09-02T19:11:57-04:00","changed":"2026-09-02T20:32:30-04:00","custom":{"odu-worktree":".worktrees/run-dies-with-host","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/odu/pull/98"}}
